# 3. Practical checklist

When writing generic JavaScript/TypeScript code, handle:

```text
Runtime:
- null / undefined
- empty arrays / empty objects
- sparse arrays
- array-like and iterable inputs
- NaN, -0, BigInt, Symbol
- boxed primitives
- this binding
- prototype pollution
- async concurrency and errors

TypeScript:
- type erasure
- empty collection inference (never[])
- constraints with null/undefined
- keyof with index signatures
- variance in function types
- this types in classes
- default type parameters
- distributive conditional types
- infer with overloads
- TSX generic component syntax
- type-only imports
```

